WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.480
- We are here with Rachel McAdams, y'all,

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.313
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.313 --> 00:00:04.328
Abby Ryder Fortson, and Judy Blume.

00:00:04.328 --> 00:00:05.307
The new movie is called

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:07.080
Are You There God? It's me, Margaret.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.700
It's in theaters tomorrow.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.290
And there are some points in the movie

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:12.750
when Abby's character deals
with a group of friends

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.880
that almost feels a
little like Mean Girls.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.950
So, Rachel, my favorite thing

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.110
that I say on this show is I love,

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.340
you're one of my favorite
actors of our generation

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.640
because you go from Regina
George to a detective

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.900
to a mom in this movie,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.610
and you play a wide range of characters,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.530
which I find interesting.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.670
Are you purposeful with that?

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.820
Like in choosing what
roles you choose to do?

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:33.840
- I try to be,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:34.673
yeah.
- Yeah?

00:00:34.673 --> 00:00:38.280
- I think it lends to better performance.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.660
You know, if you're not bored,

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.710
you're not repeating yourself.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.543
- [Kelly] Yeah, (indistinct).

00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:42.376
There's, you know, you're like,

00:00:42.376 --> 00:00:43.209
I don't quite understand this.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.180
I'm gonna' have to work
really hard to figure it out.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.230
- Yeah.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.450
- And you know, for me,
variety's the spice of life,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.180
like I'm not a creature of habit at all.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.013
- Yeah.

00:00:52.013 --> 00:00:53.730
- Love to go around the
world, see different places.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.563
- Yeah.

00:00:54.563 --> 00:00:55.709
- It's something different every day.

00:00:55.709 --> 00:00:58.830
I'm just, that's just
the way I'm geared, so.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.820
And like you said,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.690
to get to live many lifetimes in one

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.430
is one of the best things that,

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:07.260
I don't know if you feel
that way as a writer as well.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.093
- You do.

00:01:08.093 --> 00:01:09.780
- I was just gonna' say
that when you're writing,

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.695
you are living, you know.

00:01:11.695 --> 00:01:12.556
- (indistinct).

00:01:12.556 --> 00:01:13.800
- You are having all of these experiences

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.300
and you are living other lives.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.133
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:16.966
- [Rachel] Yeah.

00:01:16.966 --> 00:01:18.420
- And it in a way, it's
like acting, you know?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.253
- Right.

00:01:19.253 --> 00:01:22.320
- Because I, when I was young,
I wanted to be an actor,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.777
but I never trained or did anything.

00:01:23.777 --> 00:01:24.610
(Abby laughing)

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.443
But-

00:01:25.443 --> 00:01:26.276
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:26.276 --> 00:01:30.180
- Writing fulfills that
because I am every character.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.910
- Mm-hmm. I think writing songs, same way.

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:33.743
Yeah.

00:01:33.743 --> 00:01:34.576
Even if it's about you,

00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:35.640
it's like different chapters of your life.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:36.473
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:36.473 --> 00:01:38.340
I think that writing is so therapeutic.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.320
Is that one of the reasons
why you love to write?

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:41.850
It's therapeutic for me.

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.320
- It was, it changed my life

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.490
and it saved my life and-

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.323
- [Kelly] Yeah, me too.

00:01:45.323 --> 00:01:46.770
- came along at just the right time.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.603
- Yeah.

00:01:47.603 --> 00:01:48.600
I feel very fortunate

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.460
'cause not everybody has that outlet.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.470
And I feel very fortunate to have it.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.950
- It was great for me.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:53.783
It was.
- Yeah.

00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:55.061
It's great for us too, turns out.

00:01:55.061 --> 00:01:55.894
(women laughing)

00:01:55.894 --> 00:01:57.060
Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.113
Thank you as well.

